  "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/calypsonet/keyple-demo-ticketing/tarball/26.11.13",
  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/calypsonet/keyple-demo-ticketing/zipball/26.11.13",
  "body": "### Added\r\n- Functional documentation published online at each release (https://calypsonet.github.io/keyple-demo-ticketing/), by the CI from the HTML of the latest release, instead of by hand; skipped for the repositories without a `gh-pages` branch (as the internal repository, whose releases run the release workflow of this repository).\r\n- Validation and Inspection applications: Famoco FX207 terminal, its SAM being accessed with the Android OMAPI plugin.\r\n### Changed\r\n- Sales clients: home screen with two buttons, \"Load tickets\" and \"Personalize a card\" (instead of a single \"Contactless card\" button, the personalization being in the settings menu), and the version of the application; the settings icon opens the server settings directly. Icons of the buttons derived from Material Symbols (see [NOTICE](NOTICE.md)): a transit ticket for the loading, and a contactless card being reset for the personalization (instead of a generic card and a SIM card), with the same dimensions in both clients.\r\n- Sales clients: server settings with the state of the server right below the settings, on the same row as the \"Server state\" button, with a colored status light (\"Not checked\", \"Checking…\", \"Server ready\", \"Server not ready\").\r\n- Version of the application displayed once, in the bottom right corner of the first screen: terminal selection for the Validation and Inspection applications (no longer on their settings screen), home screen for the Sales clients.\r\n- Name of the application below the Keyple logo of the top bar, on every screen, in the style of the launcher icon (colored initial): \"Validation\", \"Inspection\", \"Sales\", and \"Sales Interop\" for the multiplatform client.\r\n- Sales clients: same back arrow in the top bar (arrow instead of a chevron in the Android client, dark blue in both).\r\n- Multiplatform sales client: default server `http://192.168.0.1:8080`, as the Android client.\r\n- Multiplatform sales client: after a loading, return to the card reading for the next ticket (instead of the home screen), as the Android client.\r\n- Sales clients: warning on the screen waiting for the card to personalize, \"Warning\" then \"All the content of the\r\n  card will be reset.\" (and, on iOS, in the NFC dialog).\r\n- Multiplatform sales client: same messages as the Android client, the instructions and the progress messages being specific to each operation (reading, loading, personalization, also in the NFC dialog of iOS), and the errors being \"Server error\" and \"An error occurred\" (instead of \"Communication error\" and \"Unexpected error\"); the server returns the names and descriptions of the contracts as displayed by the Android client (\"Forbidden\", \"Unknown\", \"1 trip left\", \"From … to …\").\r\n### Fixed\r\n- Sales clients: automatic return of the result screens on the terminals pausing the screen while it stays visible (for example, the Bluebird terminals), and bar of the remaining time displayed also when the animations of the system are disabled or shortened.\r\n- Validation application: result displayed during its whole delay on the terminals pausing the screen while it stays visible (instead of being dismissed when the screen resumes).\r\n- Android applications: animations played also when the animations of the system are disabled (as on some terminals), instead of being frozen on their last frame.\r\n- Documentation: the plugins of the Bluebird and Arrive terminals are open source, built with the library of the terminal manufacturer; only the storage card libraries are on request, for CNA members.\r\n- Icons of the Sales applications (Android, multiplatform on Android and iOS): \"Sales\" instead of \"Remote\", the former name of the demo. The desktop version of the multiplatform client gets the same icon, for its window and its installers.\r\n- Icons of the Validation and Inspection applications: actual images instead of Git LFS pointers, Git LFS being no longer used by the repository.\r\n- Same application names everywhere (\"Keyple Demo — Sales\", \"Keyple Demo — Validation\", \"Keyple Demo — Inspection\"): titles of the documentation, and name of the Sales dashboard when installed as a web application.\r\n### Upgraded\r\n- `keyple-java-bom`: `2026.10.14` -> `2026.11.10` (`keyple-card-calypso-java-lib` `3.3.1` and `keyple-plugin-android-omapi-java-lib` `2.1.2`)."
